    "result_text": "Build is green (Maven exit 0, `BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests pass).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented shared-household support for `POST /api/owners`. The `sharesHousehold` request flag already existed (it made `CheckHouseholdUnique` skip the same-lastName/same-address duplicate rejection). The new piece was assigning and returning a stable shared `householdId`.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`AssignHousehold`** (new function, `rest/function/owner/AssignHousehold.java`) \u2014 when the request opts in with `sharesHousehold: true`, derives a deterministic identifier from the normalized last name + address (`SHA-256(lastName|address)`, first 16 upper-case hex chars) and stamps it on the new owner **and** every existing owner in that same household, so both sides report the same value. Uses the same case/whitespace normalization as `CheckHouseholdUnique`. No id is assigned when the flag isn't set.\n\n2. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired `assignHousehold` into the pipeline (after `build`, before `assignCustomerCode`, under `govern: [ transaction ]`).\n\n3. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added a persisted `householdId` field (`@Column(name = \"household_id\")`) with getter/setter, mirroring `customerCode`.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `householdId` as a read-only field on the `Owner` response schema. The generated `OwnerDto` picks it up and MapStruct auto-maps it by name (same as `customerCode`).\n\n5. **DB schemas** \u2014 added a `household_id` column to the owners table in all four schemas (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres; the test profile uses hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`), and appended the matching trailing `NULL` to the column-less seed inserts in the hsqldb and mysql `data.sql` files (h2/postgres already use explicit column lists).\n\nThe acceptance test `coreJoinersShareHouseholdId` \u2014 which creates two `sharesHousehold` owners at an existing owner's address and asserts both return the same non-blank `householdId` \u2014 passes, along with the full suite.",
